<title>PHILIPPINES: Rains a boon to Philippine rice and corn farmers.</title>
<headline>Rains a boon to Philippine rice and corn farmers.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The three-days of torrential rains that swamped Luzon island in the northern Philippines benefitted farmers, the Agriculture Department said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The downpour was generally beneficial to rice and corn farmers to start land preparation, except for some tobacco and vegetable farmers whose crops were slightly affected,&quot; Agriculture undersecretary Domingo Panganiban said in a report.</p>
<p>Panganiban said the government will send equipment for drying newly harvested unmilled rice in central Luzon provinces.</p>
<p>The rice harvest has only just ended in area, the country's rice bowl. Plantings are likely to begin again this month.</p>
<p>At least 29 people died and thousands were rendered homeless due to floodings.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
